WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Speaker 1: Well, we're starting with two stories&nbsp;
from Texas today, and nothing really says the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:13.200
Christmas spirit, like Texas sending busses&nbsp;
of migrants to deathly cold temperatures at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:19.560
Kamala Harris's house. And that's exactly what&nbsp;
took place. And yet Texas has real problems to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:25.680
deal with, specifically the fact that they have&nbsp;
another power emergency. This is not a show from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:32.100
last year. Texas having another power emergency&nbsp;
for more or less the exact same reasons that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.600
have in the past. We're going to get to that,&nbsp;
though. Let's start with the migrant story. New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:43.500
York Times reporting busses of migrants arrive&nbsp;
at Kamala Harris's home on Christmas Eve. About&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:49.440
130 migrants from Texas were bused to the vice&nbsp;
president's home on one of the coldest Christmas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:56.160
Eves on record in the nation's capital. This&nbsp;
is a good article by Stephanie Ly that explains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.580
what took place. Over 100 migrants arrived near&nbsp;
Kamala Harris's home Saturday evening, one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:07.800
the chilliest Christmas Eves on record. Volunteers&nbsp;
anticipated three busses with about 130 migrants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:12.780
to arrive in New York on Christmas Day. The busses&nbsp;
were rerouted to the Washington area because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:18.660
road closures and frigid conditions. Migrants&nbsp;
arrived in Washington after a 36 hour journey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:24.120
some with little more than a T-shirt or&nbsp;
a light blanket. The mutual aid group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.540
helped coordinate travel and housing&nbsp;
for them, provided food, coats, shoes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:33.120
other warm articles. Temperatures plunged below&nbsp;
20 degrees. The mutual aid groups said the busses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.880
were set by the Texas Division of Emergency&nbsp;
Management following the directive of Governor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.780
Greg Abbott's office. I don't have to tell you&nbsp;
whether he's a Democrat or Republican. You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.440
from what he did, quote, they've been doing&nbsp;
this for a few months now. It's all for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:53.220
spectacle. The cruelty is the point. It's awful to&nbsp;
use people in this manner for political reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:02.700
We have video and as you will see here, folks&nbsp;
arriving as you see some some are wearing shorts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:09.540
quite literally shorts. The temperatures got below&nbsp;
20 degrees, busses being unloaded. And this is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:14.340
political stunt. It is farcical. It is disgusting.&nbsp;
It's also dangerous. It puts people in danger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:19.140
because of the temperatures. We have another video&nbsp;
here as well. You see the clock 10 p.m. there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:27.060
busses arriving. People have been handed blankets,&nbsp;
at least some of them have. But you do see folks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:35.760
very much under dressed and it got very, very&nbsp;
cold in the northeast on Christmas Eve. The White&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:43.260
House is assailing Texas Governor Abbott per a&nbsp;
report from Reuters writing the White House on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:48.240
Monday accused Texas Governor Greg Abbott of&nbsp;
endangering lives after busloads of migrants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:56.160
from the southwest border in Texas were dropped&nbsp;
near Vice President Kamala Harris home in DC. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:01.320
Republican. Abbott has not acknowledged the drop&nbsp;
and his office has not claimed responsibility.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:12.660
Yeah. So what do we say? These are people who are&nbsp;
prioritizing their own agendas over the well-being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:18.840
and safety of others. And it's nothing short of&nbsp;
disgusting and absurd. People's lives are being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:25.200
put at risk. People woefully unprepared for the&nbsp;
temperatures that slammed the Northeast over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:30.720
holiday weekend. And they're being used as&nbsp;
political pawns. So, number one, we should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:36.420
recognize that these are human beings. They are&nbsp;
looking for safety. They're looking for a better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:42.180
life for themselves and their families. They don't&nbsp;
come to the United States willy nilly. Remember,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:49.800
many of them are leaving families and the only&nbsp;
homes that they have known to take a risk and to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:58.200
try to make a living. Now, remember, they are both&nbsp;
lazy and taking our jobs away. So they're lazily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:04.080
taking all of our jobs by working. All of those&nbsp;
stories are completely pathetic and inconsistent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:10.560
We know that. But these are people who are making&nbsp;
life altering decisions to try to better their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:17.400
circumstances. And there are folks like Texas&nbsp;
Republicans more than it's not even willing eager&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:26.280
to exploit them. Secondly, when governors do&nbsp;
this, Abbott, DeSantis, etc., not only does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:33.240
it fly in the face of basic human compassion&nbsp;
and decency, it often actually is misstating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:38.580
or misunderstanding the legal status of many of&nbsp;
these folks. I don't yet know the legal status of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:43.860
these hundred and 30 individuals. Oftentimes the&nbsp;
term migrant is used and then it's often replaced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:50.520
with illegal immigrant. But in a prior busing&nbsp;
stunt where migrants were bused to the north,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:56.460
they were folks who were actually they they&nbsp;
requested asylum and their cases were being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:01.800
processed and they were not actually here. What&nbsp;
we would define as illegally per the law, per&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:08.760
asylum law. And so understand that very often it's&nbsp;
not even accurately making the very deranged and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:16.440
inhuman point that they are trying to make. Last&nbsp;
thing, Americans are actually in agreement on many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:21.180
aspects of the immigration debate, particularly.&nbsp;
If you were six when you were brought here by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:26.760
your undocumented immigrant parents and from&nbsp;
age 6 to 20, you grew up in the United States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:32.820
went to school in the United States, etc. It&nbsp;
would be insanely cruel and illogical to send&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:39.000
that individual who was six when they came&nbsp;
here and is now 20 back to their country,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.200
which isn't even really their country anymore.&nbsp;
And in fact, I came to the U.S. legally when I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:51.600
was five and legally or illegally. My upbringing,&nbsp;
my schooling, my acculturation was in the United&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:56.340
States. Had I been brought here by my parents&nbsp;
illegally at age five to say when I was 20 in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.340 --> 00:06:02.940
the middle of college, you've got to go back&nbsp;
to Argentina would be extraordinarily inhumane.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:09.300
And that is something that most Americans agree&nbsp;
with. And yet we are unable to make progress on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:14.100
that. We've talked about why there are political&nbsp;
factions at play and on and on and on. Lastly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:22.020
really lastly, these bussing stunts will probably&nbsp;
have unintended consequences. And what I mean by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:29.160
that is you send migrants to states and sometimes&nbsp;
they're not even told until they arrive that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:36.780
is happening. So it puts an additional strain&nbsp;
on local resources and it arguably exacerbates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:42.900
difficult situations that the migrants find&nbsp;
themselves in. Okay. So you're irresponsibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:48.360
in short sighted, Lee, to get headlines doing&nbsp;
something which will actually make the problem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:54.060
worse that you're trying to solve. Because if the&nbsp;
migrants were able to stay or go to a place that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:59.940
was actually prepared and resource to receive&nbsp;
them, it would have a dramatically lower impact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:04.680
on those communities. Nobody's saying there is&nbsp;
no impact when people arrive in a community,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:11.820
but by deliberately choosing to willy&nbsp;
nilly at 10 p.m., bused folks to a place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.760
that isn't even expecting them, you're&nbsp;
actually just making the problem worse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:20.640
So this is what Texas spent Christmas doing.&nbsp;
And meanwhile, look at what else is going on

